Three frames...?

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:54.050
That's a tenth of a second, right?

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.960
He can tell even that?

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:00.220
Okay, next. The narrator for the mini segment.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.390
Huh? R-Right!

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:09.020
We'll record, but it's just a dry run.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.810
R-Right, I'm ready.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:21.140
Now, let's take a break and look at some famously
strange sights in these beautiful landscapes!

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:25.080
Hello, I'm Slothy the sloth.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.140
Okay, stop.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.220
Oh...

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:34.650
Let's see... I'm not sure where to start...

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:37.160
l-l'm sorry!

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:40.450
Hello.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:43.800
Oh, Atsumari-san, hello.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:46.220
Thank you for working with our Ichinose.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.900
Well, it should go kind of like that.

00:17:57.900 --> 00:17:59.150
R-Right!

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:02.060
Well, I'll go prepare the rest
of the script, so please wait.

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:07.280
Excuse me, Machi-san. I'm sorry,
but we need to take a 15-minute break.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.060
Okay.

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:20.170
It's okay. I was like that
when I first started, too.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:20.740
Huh?!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:24.180
A script you've never seen before
and a video you've never seen before.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.500
It's hard <i>not</i> to be flustered by that.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:30.310
For live morning broadcasts,

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:34.270
there were times in the past where the script
still wasn't ready 5 minutes before show time.

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:36.760
Five minutes before?! For a live show?

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:40.820
Sometimes I'd suddenly be told to ad-Iib, too.

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:43.150
And sometimes the director would
whisper what to say in my ear,

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:46.270
and I'd have to do the narration like that.

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.770
Whoa...

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:52.290
But that's part of getting used to it...

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.480
...for everyone.

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:59.880
I see. No one starts out being good at it.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:05.630
Machi-san experienced a variety of situations,
studied, and worked hard.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:07.970
That's why...

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.020
Oh!

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:13.270
Once, there was a newbie who said,
"Hi, I'm a giraffe!"

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:15.500
even though it was
a gorilla on screen...

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:19.770
Thanks for waiting, Machi-san.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:21.320
Oh, coming.

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:26.390
What?! What happened to that newbie, Machi-san?

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:35.150
Okay, let's do it while recording.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:36.520
Okay!

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:47.660
Now, let's take a break and look at some famously
strange sights in these beautiful landscapes!

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:52.060
Hello, I'm Slothy the sloth.

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:57.860
The zoo I live in is thriving
today, too. Ups-a-daisy.

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:05.170
Active kids might like this
better than the view.

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.260
Ack!

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:12.080
You went way over, but it's a lot better.

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:14.940
As long as you do it in the
time allotted, it'll be fine.

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:17.940
Okay!

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:21.380
All right, one more time.

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:22.610
Please!

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:31.200
Now, let's take a break and look at some famously
strange sights in these beautiful landscapes!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.310
Good work today.

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:38.210
Good work tod-Huh?

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.210
Atsumari-san?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:43.270
I watched you at your first narration job.

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:44.800
Oh, um, uh...

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:49.450
I'm sorry for the trouble
caused by Ichinose Futaba.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:52.320
Don't worry about it. Well, I'm leaving first.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:53.440
Good work today.

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:57.610
Good work today! Thank you very much!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:02.360
Oh, Ichinose-san, I'll tell you the
rest of the gorilla story next time.

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:04.760
Okay!

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:14.930
I was just thinking that Machi-san was amazing...

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:16.680
What, after all this time?

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:18.640
Yeah, but...

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:24.230
After being in the same studio with him,
I feel like I saw that even more...

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:26.420
I learned a lot today!

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:30.820
It's good to have work
where people see your face,

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.850
but I hope you get more work like this, too.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:34.220
Yes!

00:21:45.210 --> 00:21:49.510
Ichinose Futaba, on the road home after work...

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:52.840
Her days as a seiyuu are filled with hardships,

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:57.100
but the street lights glitter
like they're shining on her path...

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:02.600
And the stars shine down like blessings!

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:05.980
Just kidding.

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:32.720
Hey, Ichigo, how did you do that sparkle
thing at the event the other day?

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:35.010
Huh? Oh, you make a cute pose
with your hands and do this-

00:22:35.010 --> 00:22:36.970
Wow! Um, like this?

00:22:36.970 --> 00:22:40.000
You two are amazing! I'll try to... Like this?

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:40.340
Huuh?

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:41.980
That's no good! Like this!

00:22:41.980 --> 00:22:43.230
Do it this way!

00:22:43.230 --> 00:22:45.460
Huh? Why? I can't do it at all...!

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:48.400
iyoiyo CD debyuu desu
It's finally time for our CD debut

00:22:48.400 --> 00:22:52.590
chimeido hikui kedo zenryoku de
Not many people know us, but we'll do our best

00:22:52.590 --> 00:22:56.090
shabette utatte odoru n desu
Talking, singing, and dancing

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:58.120
And now, we have a request!

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:01.760
From <i>Martian Successor Nadesico</i>,
it's "You Get to Burning"!

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:04.000
you get to burning
You get to burning

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:09.160
kimi rashiku hoko rashiku mukatte yo
Be yourself, be proud, and face them head on

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:13.440
muchuu ni natta hibi ga yume no
The days you spend running after your dream

00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:16.140
kakera sa
make up a part of that dream

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:17.800
Now, let's get fired up!

00:23:17.800 --> 00:23:19.720
One, two, three and go!
